  "implementation": [
    "Core media leases optionally expose opaque packet file custody. Synchronous paired target policy can opt into that custody while other policy implementations retain independent fresh authorization. Data/ingress/ordinary-forward invocation contexts remain separate and explicitly pass no packet context.",
    "Each mixer Segment indexes its own currently owned source lease, not a different source or target grant. Recipient admission retains the original source, route, consumer, scene, subscription and frame-age checks. No context or permission reader is added to QueuedMedia.",
    "After dequeue Core obtains a new current source lease, then derives each current recipient using only that same active source lease context. Every refused attempt drops its readers before waiting. Original200ms age, source expiry, cancellation and current binding/subscription guards remain enforced.",
    "Service Fresh exposes only its NativeMediaRead as opaque context. Current paired-native policy requires that exact actual source descriptor/owner/activation and then calls Store::try_native_media_read_under, which validates current exact namespace/runtime ownership, complete current scope coverage and minimum expiry without reader fallback. Fresh recipient facts, subscription permission, source match and current target owner/activation remain checked.",
    "The existing initial/SIP/replacement-specific current policy paths retain their independent fresh checks. No HTTP/native wire envelope, operation ID, peer/receiver count, command bound, scope set or decoded-frame threshold changed.",
    "Upstream changes are tracked in gate6-native-packet-custody.patch with a source-lock digest. A fresh prepared175 tree preserves4038 unchanged file mtimes; only the recorded five upstream files differ. No prepared source bytes were edited directly."
  ],
